1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,240
AI agents are starting to spend company money.

2
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:09,185
They buy software, pay suppliers, settle customer claims.

3
00:00:09,235 --> 00:00:12,655
So every CFO will ask the same question:

4
00:00:12,705 --> 00:00:14,650
who is holding the pen?

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:19,174
Today a company has two bad options.

6
00:00:19,224 --> 00:00:24,405
Hand an agent a card number and hope it behaves:

7
00:00:24,455 --> 00:00:27,675
no auditor will sign that off.

8
00:00:27,725 --> 00:00:34,650
Or approve every cent yourself, and the agent saves you nothing.

9
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,606
Purser is the third option.

10
00:00:37,656 --> 00:00:42,668
Every agent gets its own company card and its own on-chain

11
00:00:42,718 --> 00:00:46,072
mandate, with limits the CFO sets once.

12
00:00:46,122 --> 00:00:49,650
Anything new waits for the CFO's Face ID.

13
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:55,207
Meet Northwind Outdoor, a retailer that runs three agents.

14
00:00:55,257 --> 00:01:01,275
Its operations agent buys warehouse software on its own Airwallex card:

15
00:01:01,325 --> 00:01:02,044
approved.

16
00:01:02,094 --> 00:01:06,745
Then it wants the Pro plan, forty-five euros, on a card

17
00:01:06,795 --> 00:01:08,369
that allows thirty.

18
00:01:08,419 --> 00:01:10,249
Airwallex declines it:

19
00:01:10,299 --> 00:01:13,839
the bank enforces the limit, not a prompt.

20
00:01:13,889 --> 00:01:15,890
The agent asks for more.

21
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:20,505
The CFO sees the exact terms on the phone and approves

22
00:01:20,555 --> 00:01:21,616
with Face ID.

23
00:01:21,666 --> 00:01:26,659
The new limit syncs to the card, the purchase goes through,

24
00:01:26,709 --> 00:01:29,650
and every step is in the audit log.

25
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:31,567
Now a real bill:

26
00:01:31,617 --> 00:01:36,093
eighteen hundred and fifty euros from the manufacturer.

27
00:01:36,143 --> 00:01:41,360
The finance agent reads the invoice, checks the balances and the

28
00:01:41,410 --> 00:01:44,570
reserve floors, and takes a live quote.

29
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:49,672
It converts only the euros that are missing, three hundred and

30
00:01:49,722 --> 00:01:52,964
seventy, and prepares the SWIFT payment.

31
00:01:53,014 --> 00:01:57,572
The CFO approves the exact amount, the rate and the most

32
00:01:57,622 --> 00:01:58,807
the fee may be.

33
00:01:58,857 --> 00:02:00,288
Airwallex pays it:

34
00:02:00,338 --> 00:02:04,650
status PAID, with the approval's hash in the payment.

35
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:09,694
Agents also pay per request on Metal, a few cents at

36
00:02:09,744 --> 00:02:13,284
a time, under mandates that live on chain.

37
00:02:13,334 --> 00:02:19,096
When the supplier doubles its price, the agent's own account refuses

38
00:02:19,146 --> 00:02:20,121
the payment:

39
00:02:20,171 --> 00:02:24,053
nothing moves, and the customer isn't charged.

40
00:02:24,103 --> 00:02:29,437
Purser prices two options, Opus reviews them, and the CFO picks

41
00:02:29,487 --> 00:02:29,779
one.

42
00:02:29,829 --> 00:02:31,745
Then a customer claims:

43
00:02:31,795 --> 00:02:34,223
our agent never ordered this.

44
00:02:34,273 --> 00:02:38,497
Northwind's Dispute desk checks what it can prove:

45
00:02:38,547 --> 00:02:44,650
every order the customer's agent signed, every payment verified on chain

46
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:47,214
inside the customer's mandate.

47
00:02:47,264 --> 00:02:49,009
Twelve out of twelve.

48
00:02:49,059 --> 00:02:54,650
Not refunded, with a report the customer can check for themselves.

49
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:59,423
Sometimes the CFO just needs something done:

50
00:02:59,473 --> 00:03:04,355
book a flight to Berlin, at most a hundred and fifty

51
00:03:04,405 --> 00:03:04,924
euros.

52
00:03:04,974 --> 00:03:11,562
Purser checks it against the policy, and Airwallex issues a single-use

53
00:03:11,612 --> 00:03:12,036
card:

54
00:03:12,086 --> 00:03:17,442
airlines only, a hundred and fifty euros, until that day.

55
00:03:17,492 --> 00:03:19,813
The booking goes through.

56
00:03:19,863 --> 00:03:22,469
A second charge is declined:

57
00:03:22,519 --> 00:03:24,650
the card closed itself.

58
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:26,559
Why trust it?

59
00:03:26,609 --> 00:03:31,190
Code decides; the models only read and advise.

60
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:37,835
Our red team ran thirty-four attacks, from fake invoices to prompt

61
00:03:37,885 --> 00:03:40,855
injection to forged approvals:

62
00:03:40,905 --> 00:03:43,775
all thirty-four were blocked.

63
00:03:43,825 --> 00:03:48,104
Above a threshold, two people must approve.

64
00:03:48,154 --> 00:03:52,836
One Face ID freezes every agent and every card.

65
00:03:52,886 --> 00:03:57,770
Eighteen end-to-end scenarios replay as expected.

66
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:03,206
The AI costs about nine cents per thousand euros paid.

67
00:04:03,256 --> 00:04:09,650
And every payment lands in the books, double-entry and balanced.

68
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:14,874
Every company will soon run agents that spend.

69
00:04:14,924 --> 00:04:21,106
Purser lets them move at machine speed, while the finance team

70
00:04:21,156 --> 00:04:22,513
keeps the pen.

71
00:04:22,563 --> 00:04:27,338
Built on Airwallex and Metal, powered by Claude.

72
00:04:27,388 --> 00:04:29,650
Every euro has a proof.
